The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed (6366e073). I had to use git add -f because session_plan/ is gitignored. It is shorter than planned: I ran out of context before the competitor and yopedia research, so that step was skipped.

Main finding: #965 reproduces on the current build. I pointed the binary at a local stub server that returns 404. yoyo -p "hi" exits 0 with a 1-byte stdout, and adding --output-format json also exits 0 and writes no JSON. The cause is in src/prompt.rs at lines 940–950. The last else branch for non-retriable errors prints the red error: line but doesn't record the error the way the neighbouring branches do. So the turn reports success, the configured fallback provider is never tried, and the exit-1 path is never reached. The stream-json loop already records this error, so the gap is only on the normal display path. I recommend #965 as Task 1: the likely fix is one line setting self.fatal_error in that branch. The tests should check that 400, 401 and 404 exit 1 and produce is_error: true in JSON, and that a successful run still exits 0.

Other things the planner should know:
• **Stale issues to close:** #742 (fixed in `8d1f0ff3` but still open), #773 (its revert receipt), #959 (its work landed in `ecf15eee`) and #960 (an empty fallback task, which failed during the model/config breakage).
• **Unreviewed work:** #958 is the Day 210 diff that was accepted without the evaluator ever judging it. Reviewing it would make a cheap second task.
• **Pattern behind recent failures:** three sessions today looked green but produced nothing. #965 is the product-side cause: the loop's scripts have to scan the error text precisely because yoyo's exit code can't be trusted.
